  "evidence": [
    "Pinned original word 0x93E8EC equals NetDaemonNet original base0x93CD90 + lock_state_0x1B2C + trailing_words_0x14 + index7*4, offset0x1B5C. Distinct readiness word0x93E8E0 is trailing index4.",
    "NetDaemon ctor/init/reset, DONE TURN/NEXT TURN handlers and newgame reset already write genuine lock_state_[0].trailing_words_[7]; standalone ConsoleFactionsWaitingMask duplicates the same original storage.",
    "Scope includes NetDaemon ownership and affected Console set_move/end_my_turn, game net_end_of_turn/net_control_turn, faction wait_loop/commlink_attempter, MainMenu check, MultiWin draw_time and net_not_my_turn callers plus their source-extracted controls. Header storage/accessor changes must preserve existing object layout.",
    "Use native guarded object_writer.replace_object_records to transport the existing v1 object identity into v3 member NetDaemonNet.lock_state_[0].trailing_words_[7] after fresh COFF/CodeView verification; no hand-edited mapping, invented extent or duplicate parent identity.",
    "Pinned withdraw path53611D loads absolute93E8EC at53612C after log_say and stores it at536172; local approval path535097 also uses absolute93E8EC at5350B3/5350FA. Preserve singleton storage rather than an arbitrary passed daemon. Current withdraw helper snapshots before logging: correct this genuine callback-order gap while consolidating ownership."
  ],
  "intent": "Consolidate the original faction waiting mask into genuine NetDaemon lock-state storage and correct all duplicate-alias callers together. Preserve original bit operations, sentinel, reads across callbacks, original object identity and historical matching obligations; no bug fixes.",
